1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,527
This tree grew from a single seed.

2
00:00:02,707 --> 00:00:05,647
Every fork, side shoot, and flower came from blocks.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,335
Every active tip runs this stack once per generation.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,227
First it turns slightly toward the sun.

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:21,137
Then it grows a new segment, one point two eight metres long.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,657
When a bud reaches age seven, it splits into two tips.

7
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,017
They grow twenty-five degrees to either side.

8
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,747
The original tip ends its turn, and the new buds start at age zero.

9
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:43,441
The split gives the tree its basic shape. This adds variation.

10
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:50,070
Each time a bud reaches this block, it has a fifteen percent chance
to sprout a side shoot and keep growing.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:03,034
A flower needs two things. The bud must be at least six generations old,
and another branch must be within half a metre.

12
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,992
When both conditions are met, the tip stops growing and blooms.

13
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,003
The fifteen percent roll controls side shoots. Crowding triggers flowers.

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,593
There's a separate rule for wood that's already grown.

15
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:27,277
Once a segment reaches age twenty, it gets thirty percent thicker
and turns brown.

16
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:33,242
Now let's grow it.

17
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:38,363
Watch the first forks form, then the gaps fill with side shoots.

18
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:42,955
As the canopy gets crowded, flowers start appearing among the leaves.

19
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:55,671
Scrub back to the first fork, then return to the finished canopy.

20
00:01:55,851 --> 00:01:58,055
A fresh run rolls the side shoots again.
